aint N + P = 10 ≠ 12.50 is either ignored or the total is mis-remembered. The covering principle is that both constraints must be satisfied simultaneously; the skeptical stance here is a degenerate solution that satisfies only the difference constraint.","optional_refs":["74fde5320d6c79520ea82d22a3e0c25a5ecc8e0cb50c3197058c5a3b0ecd2845","8531c10a700ee412f5ba855692f060bdf9a9a5ee17bec796c657c18ce062b187"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.05},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"The pen costs $11.25, from inverting the direction of the $10 difference so that P = N + 10 (pen costs more than notebook) while keeping N + P = 12.50.","counterconditions":["If the sentence is parsed as 'notebook costs $10 more than pen' (N above P), the inversion is corrected.","If the plausibility of a pen costing $11.25 and a notebook $1.25 is questioned, the inversion is caught."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"If the comparative is inverted so the pen costs $10 more than the notebook, then P = N + 10 and N + P = 12.50 gives N + (N + 10) = 12.50, so 2N = 2.50, N = 1.25, P = 11.25. The covering principle is the directionality of 'more than': the notebook is above the pen, not the reverse.","optional_refs":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.1},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"The price of the pen is underdetermined unless we specify whether 'costs $10 more' is gross or net of tax, and whether the $12.50 is pre-tax or post-tax.","counterconditions":["If the problem is taken at face value in a pure-mathematics context (no tax), the standard solution P = 1.25 holds.","If both the $12.50 and the $10 are confirmed to be in the same denomination and scope, the underdetermination is resolved."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"An empiric stance probes whether the two constraints fully pin down the pen price under real-world pricing conventions. If the $12.50 total is tax-inclusive but the $10 difference is pre-tax, or vice versa, the system has a third free parameter (tax rate) and the pen price is not uniquely determined. The covering principle is constraint completeness: two equations pin down two unknowns only if they are independent and identically scoped.","optional_refs":["8929789f0ae19d5b1c2537f758719daf17f9908ce1fb0ca3fa0cc60fe9f2a2a3","30be11905db881ea7a4e488a8e68f34e4f6b262380bb3b1a31ceb9763a9aea81"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.05}],"simulation_proposals":[]}